 "result": "The default session is `SignedCookieSession` in `src/tessel/sessions.py`, created by `SignedCookieSessionInterface` in the same file.\n\n- **Wiring:** `SignedCookieSessionInterface.serializer` is set to the module-level `session_json_serializer = TypedCookieSerializer()` (`sessions.py:273`, `:300`). It is passed as `serializer=` when the signing serializer is built (`:316`).\n- **Serializer:** `TypedCookieSerializer` (`src/tessel/json/tag.py:219`) has `dumps` and `loads` (`:321`, `:325`). It walks the value and swaps non-JSON types for tagged one-key dicts, then reverses that on load.\n- **Per-type tag classes:** these subclass `TypeMarker` (`tag.py:60`).\n  - `TagTuple` (`:133`) handles tuples.\n  - `TagBytes` (`:159`) handles bytes.\n  - `TagDateTime` (`:205`) handles datetimes.\n  - `TagDict` (`:93`) escapes user dicts that would collide with a tag key, and `PassDict` (`:119`) and `PassList` (`:147`) pass dicts and lists through while their contents are processed.\n  - `TagMarkup` (`:173`) and `TagUUID` (`:191`) cover markup and UUIDs.\n\nEach tag class checks whether a value is its type, converts it to a tagged JSON form, and converts the tag back to the original type on load. That is how the types survive the cookie round trip.",
